    <item>
      <title>Reload Unity Panel in Ubuntu Without Restarting</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/reload-unity-panel-in-ubuntu-without-restarting/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 Nov 2024 16:29:30 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/reload-unity-panel-in-ubuntu-without-restarting/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Here is a command to reload the unity desktop notification panel, in Ubuntu, without restarting the entire system:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;killall unity-panel-service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As soon as the process is killed, a new one will be spawned, refreshing the notification panel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is useful if you have duplicate icons from frozen apps in the panel.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
